%% The workflow state machine, SIMPLIFIED for the report (Figure 3.3): the main path and the
%% two human pauses only. The complete table (22 transitions, including Failed and the edges
%% nothing fires yet) is in workflow-state-machine-full.mmd and api/Services/WorkflowTransitions.cs.

stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> Submitted : report filed

    Submitted --> AwaitingClarification : questions asked
    Submitted --> Diagnosing : no questions needed
    AwaitingClarification --> Diagnosing : reporter answered

    Diagnosing --> Strategizing : diagnosed

    Strategizing --> WorkOrderRaised : auto-approved
    Strategizing --> AwaitingManagerApproval : needs approval

    AwaitingManagerApproval --> WorkOrderRaised : approved
    AwaitingManagerApproval --> Strategizing : revision requested
    AwaitingManagerApproval --> Closed : rejected

    WorkOrderRaised --> Completed : job completed
    Completed --> AwaitingVerification : 5 days later

    AwaitingVerification --> Closed : repair held
    AwaitingVerification --> Diagnosing : repair failed

    Closed --> [*]

    note right of AwaitingClarification
        Human pause 1: the reporter
        answers on the phone
    end note

    note left of AwaitingManagerApproval
        Human pause 2: over Rs 15,000
        or a replacement needs a manager
    end note

    classDef pause fill:#E8E6FC,stroke:#5B50E8,stroke-width:2px,color:#15171C
    classDef done fill:#EEF0F3,stroke:#15171C,color:#15171C
    class AwaitingClarification,AwaitingManagerApproval pause
    class Closed done
